in{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot (-5)-(-9)\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-2+\\frac{5}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}=0.\n$$" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix form of $T$ gives us the following information:\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot (-5)-(-9)\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-2+\\frac{5}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}=0.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186259633 :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 9 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind $a+b+c,$ given that the matrix form of the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ -1 & c\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "The matrix form of the affine transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 9 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind $a+b+c,$ given that