} & =\\overset{―}{\\begin{bmatrix}-4-2\\text{i} & 7+5\\text{i} & 6+6\\text{i} \\\\ -4+5\\text{i} & 2-\\text{i} & 3 \\\\ -2-\\text{i} & 2-\\text{i} & -3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\overset{―}{-4-2\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{7+5\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{6+6\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-4+5\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{2-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{3} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-2-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{2-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{-3\\text{i}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4+2\\text{i} & 7-5\\text{i} & 6-6\\text{i} \\\\ -4-5\\text{i} & 2+\\text{i} & 3 \\\\ -2+\\text{i} & 2+\\text{i} & 3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${b}_{23}+{b}_{33}=3+3\\text{i}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186266069 :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186266069 :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $2$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $2$nd and $3$rd columns." "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $2$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $2$nd and $3$rd columns."] [:db/cas 17592186266070 :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\